%U A398748 13505211025587949473183132225,2887891038178748592057487942708522
%N A398748 Number of double total dominating sets in the n X n grid graph: vertex subsets S such that every vertex of the grid, whether in S or not, has at least two neighbors in S.
%C A398748 Double total domination is also called total {2}-domination or 2-total domination by some authors; definitions vary, and the one counted here requires |N(v) intersect S| >= 2 for every vertex v, members of S included, with N(v) the open neighborhood.
%C A398748 a(1) = 0 since an isolated vertex has no neighbors. a(2) = 1 counts only S = all four vertices, since every vertex of the 2 X 2 grid has exactly two neighbors, both of which must be chosen.
%o A398748 (Python)
%o A398748 from itertools import product
%o A398748 def a(n):
%o A398748     cells = [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(n)]
%o A398748     nb = {c: [(c[0]+d, c[1]+e) for d, e in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)) if 0 <= c[0]+d < n and 0 <= c[1]+e < n] for c in cells}
%o A398748     return sum(all(sum(x in S for x in nb[c]) >= 2 for c in cells) for S in ({c for c, b in zip(cells, bits) if b} for bits in product((0, 1), repeat=n*n)))
%Y A398748 Cf. A133515 (dominating sets of the n X n grid), A133793 (total dominating sets), A290382 (minimal dominating sets), A398747 (2-dominating sets).
%K A398748 nonn,more,new
%O A398748 1,3
